        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How much does the Life Fitness F3 cost?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On Life Fitness's store on 21 November 2026 it was $2,799 with the Go Console and $3,295 with the Track Connect 2.0 console, on sale from a $3,499 list price, with free in-home delivery and assembly. Prices change often, so check the current figure.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the weight limit on the Life Fitness F3?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Life Fitness gives a maximum user weight of 350 lb (159 kg), which is high for a folding treadmill. The machine itself weighs 264 lb.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the difference between the Life Fitness F3 and T3?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The F3 folds; the T3 does not. On Life Fitness's comparison table on 15 October 2026, the F3 had a 55 by 20-inch running surface, 10 mph and 12% incline, while the T3 had 60 by 20 inches, 12 mph and 15%, both from $3,499. Runners should prefer the T3.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Life Fitness F3 have Bluetooth?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Only with the Track Connect 2.0 console. It adds Bluetooth Low Energy, Apple GymKit and Samsung watch support, Bluetooth heart-rate straps and third-party apps over FTMS. The Go Console has no Bluetooth, apps or USB port.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is the Life Fitness F3 good for running?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For easy jogging, yes. For faster or taller runners it is limited by its 10 mph top speed and 55-inch belt. The non-folding Life Fitness T3 offers 12 mph on a 60-inch deck.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What warranty does the Life Fitness F3 have?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Life Fitness listed a lifetime warranty on the frame and Lifesprings, 10 years on the motor, 5 years on mechanical and electrical parts, 3 years on the console and 1 year on labour, as of 21 November 2026.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

